  "claim": "A compiled multi-leg FIRE/ZPL portfolio with positive fixed-point scale and posted collateral covering the per-leg rounding-mode expanded interval produces a projectable settlement receipt: holder and writer remain solvent after applying their deltas, and the deltas conserve exactly. Independent receipts compose by addition with a neutral zero receipt; finite receipt aggregation preserves bilateral solvency, exact conservation, and net-zero posted-collateral accounting, is compatible with empty, singleton, insert, commutative disjoint union, associative three-way disjoint batching, and pure relabeling of receipt indices. The expanded interval width is exactly the unexpanded width plus one tick per leg.",
